  /Subject (Coordination Knowledge Substrate \(CKS\) \204 Paper 2 derivation note B1.18 \204 formalizes the architectural commitment that higher structural levels operate over lower structural levels as content domain \(aspects ask pattern questions across constituent cells; Selves hold aspects as facets\), distinct from rigid hierarchical command-and-control, preserving lower-level autonomy while enabling higher-level reasoning.) /Title (Higher Levels Operate Over Lower Levels as Content Domain: Foundational Commitment Establishing the Inter-Level Architectural Relationship in the Coordination Knowledge Substrate Pattern) /Trapped /False
